    intro: "Turban Tying Booking for a Standout Groom Look is one of the most common requests we get from couples and families planning a wedding, and it starts with a single detail: your date, venue and guest count.",
    section1Title: "What this covers",
    section1Body: "The groom's session is treated as unhurried and detailed — kalgi, brooch or feather placement is checked against the sherwani — while the rest of the wedding party follows a faster, still-coordinated fold.",
    section2Title: "How to book",
    section2Body: "Most bookings are confirmed over WhatsApp: share the essentials, get a package recommendation, and lock in the date. No showroom visit is required unless you'd prefer one.",
    section3Title: "Who usually books this",
